<tr>
	<td width="80%" height="352"align="left" valign="top" bordercolorlight="Aqua" bordercolordark="Navy" background="imgbkgdbl.gif"><b><font size="+1">Dragon's Oath (DO) Rules:<br></font></b>
These are general rules of conduct for more please see the Charter.<br>
<br>
Honor the family name. Please remember the tag you adorn reflects the entire guild<br>
<br>
Be courteous to all. Public arguments or bashing in /shout or /ooc are unacceptable. Take it to tells, report violations or call upon an officer for assistance to help diffuse the situation. This includes Verant/EQ. There are other ways to deal with your complaints or dissatisfactions. 
Guild Chat and the DO message board is NOT to be used to air grievances. This applies to all members, officers, and leader(s). <br>
<br>
DO does not tolerate the use of foul language in guild chat, group chat, or in ooc/shouts across the zone.<br>
<br>
DO brothers and sisters are always willing to lend a hand to those in need. Please be kind when asking for assistance. 
Begging is not permitted within the guild. Requests for ports and resurrections should be addressed in tells. Seek services in your current zone before asking a member to run across Norrath to assist.<br>
<br>
Be honest in all transactions. Defrauding another member or player is
grounds for guild removal, if found guilty.<br>
<br>
Before trying to make a profit outside the guild on items you no longer need, look within the guild for those in need. Members should not accept an item they can not use.<br>
<br>
Respect all requests of the DO officers and leaders. They are to be followed even if they are on a secondary character (they must inform you of the character that is of rank)<br>
<br>
Follow all of the Verant/EQ rules/including naming policy.<br>
<br>
Members are responsible for keeping up-to-date with the content of the DO Message Board system. We use this to collaborate quests, raids, and meetings; as well as tons of useful information.<br>
<br>
<b><font size="+1">Dragon's Oath Recruitment Guidelines</font></b><br>
New member must be a season of 10 or higher. They must know the game well enough to play on their own before joining the guild. We want them to be able to give assistance, as well as receive it.<br>
<br>
The pending applicant must have 2 members speak for them and their honor. These members will send a tell to an Officer regarding the recruit.  
The potential member will post a message to the "Welcome, Potential Members." section leaving information such as: Player Name, Race, Class, Level.  Potential Member will also need to create a login on this site, add a character then select join link.  This needs to be done before anyone will get a Tag.
 <br>
<br>
The New recruit will have 7 days to try out the guild. 
